  "claim_boundary": "This proof starts from a fixed post-calc retail anchor and accepts only replay input masks per transition. The committed guest derives position, life state/timer, focus, previousFrameInput, fire-timer cadence, and a cumulative count of SpawnBullets requests. The 2,000-frame retail/reference oracle compares 46 fields, and the static audit pins 54 instruction roles through focused/unfocused callback dispatch. This is evidence for the selected no-dialogue/no-bomb/no-hit/full-speed interval, not a proof of compiler correspondence or complete writer noninterference. Bullet-slot allocation, character-specific callback geometry, collision/death, bomb execution, item interaction, dialogue transitions, ECL time-stop writers, and whole-game state remain outside the proved transition."
